WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.139
Let's go next to our caller.

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:07.770
Oh, we've got someone from the 4 1 3 area
code who's calling today from 4 1 3.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.620
Hey, let me.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:10.620
Yes, it is.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.620
Who's this?

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.920
Oh, this is Tyler.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.520
I'm originally from Belltown, Massachusetts,
but I live in Washington, D.C. now.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.039
It is cool.

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:21.320
What's going on?

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:26.189
I'm starting to hear a lot of talk about how
the government is going to use the crisis

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:28.420
in order to curtail personal freedoms.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.070
Sort of like how the Patriot Act was used.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.540
And I don't know if I'm just naive, but I'm
not super concerned about that and just wondering

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.060
what your opinion on it is.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.940
So I think that here's the here's the.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.580
So there's some truth to it, but it's not
really in the way that most people fear.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:50.080
So the way most people fear the government
using the corona virus crisis to curtail freedoms

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:58.360
are the kind of dystopian sci fi, you know,
ways of monitoring people in ways that that

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.540
that exceed what the current law allows.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.090
Or, you know, people are talking about martial
law, military in the streets and all this

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.090
type of stuff.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:12.080
What they're doing, they're already doing,
which is, for example, court systems are not

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.270
functioning at full capacity.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:20.780
So one of the things that the Trump administration
is now asking for is that habeas corpus, which

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:27.780
basically allow, determines or dictates people
can't just be held indefinitely without being

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:29.150
charged or tried.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.150
Right.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.150
You got it.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.690
There has to be a process that continues moving
forward reasonably quickly.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.250
The idea is, hey, listen.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:40.790
Courts can't really process as much as they
can normally because of the virus.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:45.110
So we should sort of just like allow people
to be indefinitely detained, even if we can't

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.700
give them a trial anytime soon.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.120
That's being done like that.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.120
It's happening now.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.490
So it is happening.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:55.940
It's just probably not in the exact way that
some people are fearful of.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:56.940
Yeah.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.340
I mean, I think we definitely have to be mindful
of that.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:05.120
But I'm hearing some people using that as
an excuse as to why we shouldn't take this

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.710
seriously and why we shouldn't tax more.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:08.710
Right.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:09.780
No, it's.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.810
The solution is that's not the solution.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:17.420
The solution would be, listen, if the justice
system can't process people, then you're going

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:22.350
to have to just like let some people go and
then, you know, you're not you're going to

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.260
have to maybe re apprehend them later.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:27.200
And some people are gonna be flight risks
and you won't be able to.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.310
But it's incumbent upon the justice system
to provide that speedy trial.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.760
And you can't say, well, you just sit in jail
indefinitely.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:40.370
So I think you're right that there are people
who are cynically coming up with the wrong

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:42.500
solution to this problem.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.670
But we want to make sure that it doesn't get
misused to minimize how much we should all

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.440
just be staying the hell home.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.440
Absolutely.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.750
Well, hey, thanks for answering my call.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:55.750
Have a great day.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:56.750
All right, Tyler, great to hear from you.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:57.310
I appreciate it.

